          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice offered below is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2014 DnD 5e Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/state-of-the-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-official",
      "heading": "Are Grung an Official Playable Race?",
      "sourceAnchor": "official",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-official-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No. The DMsGuild page for One Grung Above clarifies:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-official-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Disclaimer: Outside of a certain surrogate character, this document in no way\n\tmakes grung a legal, playable race in the D&D Adventurers League, or any\n\tother campaign where the Dungeon Master hates amphibians with an excess of\n\tapostrophes in their names… and yes if you’re not immune to poison and you\n\tmust touch the grung to heal it… you get to make a saving throw."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-official-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Between this and the mechanical issues discussed above, I do not cover the\n\tGrung in my other character optimization content."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Grung Classes (Customizable Origins)",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes-custom-origin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-classes-custom-origin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This section assumes that you’re using the option “"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Customizing Your Origin",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/tcoe/character-options#CustomizingYourOrigin"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "” rules presented in Tasha’s Cauldron of Everything. If you’re not using those rules, scroll down to the next section."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fine for melee builds, but ranged artificers generally use spells rather than\n\tweapons, so the Grung’s poison isn’t useful for them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Poison added to your attacks and Standing Leap makes difficult terrain mostly\n\ta non-issue."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "With the exception of College of Valor, bards don’t get enough attacks to\n\tmake the Grung’s poison worthwhile, and while Standing Leap and an extra skill\n\tare both nice, they’re not enough to carry a build."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Clerics don’t get enough attacks to make the Grung’s poison worthwhile, and\n\twhile Standing Leap and an extra skill are both nice, they’re not enough to\n\tcarry a build."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A circle of spores druid built around Polearm Master to capitalize on\n\tSymbiotic Entity’s damage boosts could be a good fit both mechanically and\n\tthematically for the Grung, but the Grung doesn’t solve any of the Druid’s\n\tdurability issues."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "More attacks than anyone except the Monk, and unlike the Monk they can all be\n\tpiercing damage without jumping through hoops. Go for two-weapon fighting and\n\tstab things as often and as quickly as you can manage. The extra skill helps\n\tyou be useful outside of combat, and Standing Leap trivializes difficult\n\tterrain."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "More attacks than any other character for the majority of the level range. Remember that unarmed strikes involves enemies touching your skin, which applies your poison just as well as poking them with a spear,"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Not quite as good at abusing the Grung’s poison as the Fighter, but the\n\tFighter doesn’t pull ahead until 11th level, so until then the Paladin is a\n\tfine choice for the Grung. The additional skill helps you expand beyond Face\n\tskills, and Standing Leap adds some welcome mobility."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Not quite as good at abusing the Grung’s poison as the Fighter, but the\n\tFighter doesn’t pull ahead until 11th level, so until then the Ranger is a\n\tfine choice for the Grung. The additional skill helps close the skill gap with\n\tthe Rogue, and Standing Leap adds some welcome mobility."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "As much as rogues seem like they should like poison, the Grung’s poison\n\trewards numerous attacks to try to make the low DC work, so the Rogue’s single\n\tattack (two with TWF) doesn’t help us. The extra skill and Standing Leap are\n\tnice, but that’s just not enough."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Ability score increases and one skill are really the only things that the\n\tGrung brings to the Sorcerer, and you can get that from numerous other races.\n\tAside from the novelty of being a frog person, there’s nother here worth\n\thaving."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Grung hexblades work for the same reason that most martial classes work for\n\tthe Grung, but the Hexblade can’t match the Fighter’s base number of attacks,\n\tthey’re not good at two-weapon fighting, and they don’t have something like\n\tReckless Attack to make their attacks consistently accurate. It’s workable,\n\tbut it’s not a great build."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Wizard",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-wizard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-wizard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Ability score increases and one skill are really the only things that the\n\tGrung brings to the Wizard, and you can get that from numerous other races.\n\tAside from the novelty of being a frog person, there’s nother here worth\n\thaving."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Grung Classes (Default Rules)",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes-default",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-classes-default-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This section assumes that you’re "
            },
            {
              "type": "emphasis",
              "text": "not"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " using the option “Customizing Your Origin” rules presented in Tasha’s Cauldron of Everything or the updated version of the race published in Mordenkainen’s Monsters of the Multiverse. If you are using those rules, scroll up to the previous section."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No Intelligence increase."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No Strength increase and you’re small."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Nothing especially useful for the Bard, but if you don’t focus on offensive\n\tspellcasting you can still be very effective."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No Wisdom increase."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Circle of Spores synergizes nicely with the Grung’s natural poison, but the\n\tability scores don’t work and the other racial traits aren’t very useful\n\tcompared to the Druid’s existing capabilities."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A great option because the Fighter can make more attacks than any other\n\tclass. Go for a two-weapon fighting or Crossbow Expert build for the extra\n\tattacks and attack as much as you can to try to poison enemies."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Grung makes a great monk for the same reason that they make a great fighter: good ability score increases, and multiple attacks to apply poison. Your Bonus Action attacks are almost always unarmed strikes which will apply your poison because it involves touching your skin."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Paladin doesn’t get quite as many attacks as the Fighter, so they can’t\n\tcapitalize on the Grung’s poison as well. Otherwise, the Paladin is a fine\n\toption."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Perfect ability score increases, a bonus skill, helpful movement options, and\n\tthe Grung’s poison encourages the same strategies that support Hunter’s\n\tMark."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Grung’s ability score increases and most other traits work fine for the\n\tRogue, but since rogues generally rely on one attack (sometimes two) per turn,\n\tthere’s less opportunity to capitalize on the Grung’s poison than the Ranger\n\tgets."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No Charisma increase."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-warlock",
